    "q-352630": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352630",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡x+x+2{cos}^{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡x+x+2{cos}^{2}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2\\cdot 1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{7}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{x+2}\\,{|}_{2}^{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{7+2}-\\sqrt{2+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{9}-\\sqrt{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
