    "q-352622": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352622",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{4}-1}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x=1\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{4}-1}\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x+x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{4}-1}\\frac{1}{1+x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x)\\,{|}_{0}^{{e}^{4}-1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡[1+({e}^{4}-1)]-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+0) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{4})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1) \\\\  & =4-0 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
