    "q-362509": {
      "dom_id": "step-q362509",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Using the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x,\n$$\n\nwe compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{1-{tan}^{4}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)}{(1-{tan}^{2}⁡x)(1+{tan}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{1+{tan}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
