    "q-362798": {
      "dom_id": "step-q362798",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({tan}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So, we can use the identity \n\n$$\n1+{tan}^{2}⁡x={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({tan}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x({tan}^{2}⁡x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{2}-(-2) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
