    "q-73527": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73527",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int (8{x}^{3}-2{tan}^{2}⁡x-2)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we select the identity that contains a ${tan}^{2}⁡x$ term. So we can use the identity \n\n$$\n{tan}^{2}⁡x+1={sec}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we compute the given integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (8{x}^{3}-2{tan}^{2}⁡x-2)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (8{x}^{3}-2({tan}^{2}⁡x+1))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (8{x}^{3}-2{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
