      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$\\int ({x}^{2}+5{cot}^{2}⁡x+5)\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.$ Substituting this into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+5{cot}^{2}⁡x+5)\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+5({cot}^{2}⁡x+1))\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{2}+5{csc}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-5\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
