    "q-49332": {
      "dom_id": "step-q49332",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}⁡x}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity  \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}⁡x={csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}⁡x}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{(1-{cot}^{2}⁡x)(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)}{{cot}^{2}⁡x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}(1+{cot}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
