    "q-73529": {
      "dom_id": "step-q73529",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(1-{cot}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "From the identity $1+{cot}^{2}⁡\\theta ={csc}^{2}⁡\\theta $ with $\\theta =x-\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+{cot}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ {cot}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(1-{cot}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(1-{csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}(2-{csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}2\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}{csc}^{2}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4}+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}){|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =2(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =2(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+0-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
